-- title:
--   The chart homomorphism sends X to S
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi \in W$. Write $R_\pi$ for the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W π`, namely the quotient of the two-variable formal power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, and let `mk π` be the quotient map. The chart homomorphism `chartHom π`, a ring homomorphism from the one-variable power series ring $W[[X]]$ to $R_\pi$, is the substitution of the ambient two-variable series `sAmbient` for the variable, followed by `mk π`; that substitution is legitimate by the admissibility witness `hasSubst_sAmbient W`. The assertion is that `chartHom π` takes the power series variable `PowerSeries.X` to the element `S π` of $R_\pi$, i.e. the class modulo $X_0X_1 - C(\pi)$ of the ambient series substituted for the variable is the designated element `S π` of the crossing model. No hypotheses on $W$ or $\pi$ beyond commutativity of $W$ are imposed.
--
--   This is the basic computation rule for the formal chart of the crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi)$, a local model for the completion of a modular curve of level divisible by $p$ at a supersingular point of the special fibre, where the two components cross. It is used in the constructions of isomorphisms between the crossing model and an `AdjoinRoot` presentation, in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot) and [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_ringEquiv_adjoinRoot_of_isPrecomplete).
